<title>INDIA: POLL-India SBI 6-mth net seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL-India SBI 6-mth net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Bank India's (SBI) net profit is expected to climb 16.9 percent to 7.5 billion rupees in the first half of fiscal 1997/98 (April-March), a Reuter poll consensus of 18 leading brokerages found on Wednesday.</p>
<p>State-run SBI is the country's largest commercial bank.</p>
<p>Income in the first six months to September 30, 1997 is seen rising 15.9 percent to 85.9 billion rupees from 74.1 billion in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>SBI  ----PAT seen up 16.9%, income up 15.9%</p>
<p>Average		7,493.88  6,408.00    85,937.57  74,143.40</p>
<p>High		   9,243.60		 107,200.00</p>
<p>Low		    5,210.00		  75,000.00</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk +91-22-265-9000</p>
